From 218ecc3b3ffb81266c7a57cb5e96cc3291b7ea11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 22:27:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-sunfish: don't pin-force the
 touch reset GPIO
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

touch_reset_default drove gpio8 -- the stmfts reset line, which the driver
owns via devm_gpiod_get("reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH) -- to output-high +
bias-pull-up. The pinctrl default state (applied at device-create, before
probe) and the driver gpiod then fight over the line, and the chip can be
released from reset while AVDD is still ramping. Under boot-coldplug
concurrency this intermittently leaves the controller in a bad state and the
probe's first I2C read hangs, hanging the boot until the watchdog resets it.

Drop output-high and bias-pull-up; leave function/drive-strength/bias-disable
so the driver gpiod owns the line, matching touch_irq_default.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts
index 52d20b9c7967..cf3acf2b9010 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts
@@ -913,8 +913,7 @@ touch_reset_default: touch-reset-default-state {
 		pins = "gpio8";
 		function = "gpio";
 		drive-strength = <2>;
-		bias-pull-up;
-		output-high;
+		bias-disable;
 	};
 };
 
